Done. Slice: P4.1 task app-field integrity/lifecycle tests (`done-for-review`, `Ready-to-tick: no — live Tier-2 lifecycle remains`).

**What I found and fixed:** the integrity suite I wrote exposed a genuinely broken relation graph (install-blocking `Relation field target metadata not found` plus inverse fields attached to the wrong object). Rather than codify defects, I repaired the graph:
- `label.object.ts` / `task-label.object.ts` junction ids pointed at a self/missing id.
- Moved 8 inverse O2M fields out of `project`/`milestone`/`project-member`/`time-entry` object files into standalone `src/fields/*.field.ts` on their real target objects (the `defineObject` embedded-field form omits `objectUniversalIdentifier`, so inverses landed on the FK object).
- Added the missing `task.subtasks` and `milestone.tasks` inverses.

**Tests added:** `src/lib/__tests__/task-field-integrity.test.ts` — 13 tests: id uniqueness, exact 6 objects (no duplicate junction/milestone/time-entry), every relation target object+field resolves, every relation is a symmetric M2O/O2M pair owned by its target, plus the eight task fields' contracts (project SET_NULL, select status retained, priority/estimate sets, labels CASCADE junction, subtask self-relation, blockIssue→note, humanId TEXT, time tracking).

**Checks:** `yarn test:unit` 33/33; `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0; `yarn lint` 0 errors (1 pre-existing warning); `npx oxfmt --check` clean; `npx twenty dev:build .` succeeded; manifest walk 55 fields / 0 unresolved / 0 ownership mismatches.

